== Orationes solemnes | The Solemn Prayers
R: Perlecta Passione, Prior, stans in cornu Epistolæ, dicat sequentes Orationes, sine *Dóminus vobíscum,* hoc modo.
 = The Passion having been read, the Prior, standing at the Epistle corner, says the following Orations, without *Dóminus vobíscum,* in this way.
T: ^OREMUS, dilectíssimi nobis, pro Ecclésia sancta Dei; ut eam Deus et Dóminus noster pacificáre, adunáre, et custodíre dignétur toto orbe terrárum, subjíciens ei principátus et potestátes; detque nobis, quiétam et tranquíllam vitam degéntibus, glorificáre Deum Patrem omnipoténtem.
 = Let us pray, dearly beloved, for the holy Church of God, that our Lord and God may be pleased to give it peace, to keep it united, and to guard it throughout the world, subjecting to it principalities and powers; and may He grant us, who live a quiet and peaceful life, to glorify God the Father almighty.
R: In fine hujus Orationis non respondeatur *Amen,* sed statim Sacerdos subjungat *Orémus,* et Diaconus *Flectámus génua. Leváte.* Tunc Sacerdos prosequatur Orationem
 = At the end of this Oration *Amen* is not answered, but the Priest at once adds *Orémus,* and the Deacon *Flectámus génua. Leváte.* Then the Priest continues with the Oration:
T: ^OMNIPOTENS sempitérne Deus, qui glóriam tuam ómnibus in Christo Géntibus revelásti : custódi ópera misericórdiæ tuæ; ut Ecclésia tua toto orbe diffúsa, stábili fide in confessióne tui nóminis persevéret : Per eúmdem Dóminum nostrum Jesum Christum Fílium tuum; qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus : per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum. {℟.} Amen.
 = Almighty and everlasting God, who in Christ have revealed Your glory to all nations, guard the works of Your mercy, that Your Church, spread throughout the whole world, may persevere with steadfast faith in the confession of Your name: through the same our Lord Jesus Christ Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end. {℟.} Amen.
T: ^OREMUS et pro beatíssimo Papa nostro N.; ut Deus et Dóminus noster, qui elégit eum in órdine Episcopátus, salvum atque incólumem custódiat Ecclésiæ suæ sanctæ, ad regéndum pópulum sanctum Dei : Orémus. Flectámus génua. Leváte.
 = Let us pray also for our most blessed Pope N., that our Lord and God, who chose him for the order of the episcopate, may keep him safe and unharmed for His holy Church, to govern the holy people of God. Let us pray. Let us kneel. Arise.
L: Oratio
 = Prayer
T: ^OMNIPOTENS sempitérne Deus, cujus judício univérsa fundántur; réspice propítius ad preces nostras : et eléctum nobis Antístitem tua pietáte consérva; ut christiána plebs, quæ te gubernátur auctóre, sub tanto Pontífice, credulitátis suæ méritis augeátur : Per Dóminum nostrum. {℟.} Amen.
 = Almighty and everlasting God, by whose judgement all things are founded, look favourably upon our prayers, and in Your goodness preserve the Bishop chosen for us, that the Christian people, governed by You as their author, may under so great a Pontiff increase in the merits of their faith: through our Lord. {℟.} Amen.
T: ^OREMUS et pro ómnibus Epíscopis, Presbýteris, Diacónibus, Subdiacónibus, Acólythis, Exorcístis, Lectóribus, Ostiáriis, Confessóribus, Virgínibus, Víduis, et pro omni pópulo sancto Dei : Orémus. Flectámus génua. Leváte.
 = Let us pray also for all bishops, priests, deacons, subdeacons, acolytes, exorcists, lectors, porters, confessors, virgins, widows, and for all the holy people of God. Let us pray. Let us kneel. Arise.
L: Oratio
 = Prayer
T: ^OMNIPOTENS sempitérne Deus, cujus spíritu totum corpus Ecclésiæ sanctificátur et régitur : exáudi nos pro univérsis Ordínibus supplicántes; ut grátiæ tuæ múnere, ab ómnibus tibi grádibus fidéliter serviátur : Per Dóminum... in unitáte ejúsdem Spíritus. {℟.} Amen.
 = Almighty and everlasting God, by whose Spirit the whole body of the Church is sanctified and governed, hear us as we pray for all its orders, that by the gift of Your grace You may be faithfully served by all its ranks: through our Lord... in the unity of the same Spirit. {℟.} Amen.
T: ^OREMUS et pro christianíssimo Imperatóre nostro N.; ut Deus et Dóminus noster súbditas illi fáciat omnes bárbaras natiónes ad nostram perpétuam pacem : Orémus. Flectámus génua. Leváte.
 = Let us pray also for our most Christian Emperor N., that our Lord and God may make all barbarous nations subject to him, for our perpetual peace. Let us pray. Let us kneel. Arise.
L: Oratio
 = Prayer
T: ^OMNIPOTENS sempitérne Deus, in cujus manu sunt ómnium potestátes, et ómnium jura regnórum; réspice ad Románum benígnus Impérium : ut gentes, quæ in sua feritáte confídunt; poténtiæ tuæ déxtera comprimántur : Per Dóminum. {℟.} Amen.
 = Almighty and everlasting God, in whose hand are the powers of all and the rights of all kingdoms, look graciously upon the Roman Empire, that the nations which trust in their own fierceness may be restrained by the right hand of Your power: through our Lord. {℟.} Amen.
T: ^OREMUS et pro Catechúmenis nostris, ut Deus et Dóminus noster adapériat aures præcordiórum ipsórum, januámque misericórdiæ; ut per lavácrum regeneratiónis accépta remissióne ómnium peccatórum, et ipsi inveniántur in Christo Jesu Dómino nostro : Orémus. Flectámus génua. Leváte.
 = Let us pray also for our catechumens, that our Lord and God may open the ears of their hearts and the gate of mercy, that, having received the remission of all their sins by the laver of regeneration, they also may be found in Christ Jesus our Lord. Let us pray. Let us kneel. Arise.
L: Oratio
 = Prayer
T: ^OMNIPOTENS sempitérne Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam nova semper prole fecúndas : auge fidem et intelléctum Catechúmenis nostris; ut renáti fonte baptísmatis, adoptiónis tuæ fíliis aggregéntur : Per Dóminum. {℟.} Amen.
 = Almighty and everlasting God, who ever make Your Church fruitful with new offspring, increase the faith and understanding of our catechumens, that, born again in the font of baptism, they may be joined to the children of Your adoption: through our Lord. {℟.} Amen.
T: ^OREMUS, dilectíssimi nobis, Deum Patrem omnipoténtem, ut cunctis mundum purget erróribus, morbos áuferat, famem depéllat; apériat cárceres, víncula dissólvat, peregrinántibus réditum, infirmántibus sanitátem; navigántibus portum salútis indúlgeat : Orémus. Flectámus génua. Leváte.
 = Let us pray, dearly beloved, to God the Father almighty, that He may cleanse the world of all errors, take away diseases, drive away famine, open prisons, loose chains, and grant a return to travellers, health to the sick, and a haven of safety to those at sea. Let us pray. Let us kneel. Arise.
L: Oratio
 = Prayer
T: ^OMNIPOTENS sempitérne Deus, mæstórum consolátio, laborántium fortitúdo : pervéniant ad te preces de quacúmque tribulatióne clamántium; ut omnes sibi in necessitátibus suis misericórdiam tuam gáudeant adfuísse : Per Dóminum. {℟.} Amen.
 = Almighty and everlasting God, the comfort of the sorrowful and the strength of those who toil, let the prayers of all who cry out in any trouble come before You, that all may rejoice that Your mercy has been with them in their needs: through our Lord. {℟.} Amen.
T: ^OREMUS et pro hæréticis, et schismáticis, ut Deus et Dóminus noster éruat eos ab erróribus univérsis; et ad Sanctam Matrem Ecclésiam Cathólicam atque Apostólicam revocáre dignétur : Orémus. Flectámus génua. Leváte.
 = Let us pray also for heretics and schismatics, that our Lord and God may deliver them from all their errors, and be pleased to call them back to our holy Mother the Catholic and Apostolic Church. Let us pray. Let us kneel. Arise.
L: Oratio
 = Prayer
T: ^OMNIPOTENS sempitérne Deus, qui salvas omnes, et néminem vis períre; réspice ad ánimas diabólica fraude decéptas : ut omni hærética pravitáte depósita, errántium corda resipíscant; et ad veritátis tuæ rédeant unitátem : Per Dóminum. {℟.} Amen.
 = Almighty and everlasting God, who save all men and will that none should perish, look upon the souls deceived by the fraud of the devil, that, all heretical perversity being laid aside, the hearts of those who err may repent and return to the unity of Your truth: through our Lord. {℟.} Amen.
T: ^OREMUS et pro pérfidis Judǽis, ut Deus et Dóminus noster áuferat velámen de córdibus eórum; ut et ipsi agnóscant Jesum Christum Dóminum nostrum :
 = Let us pray also for the faithless Jews, that our Lord and God may take away the veil from their hearts, that they also may acknowledge Jesus Christ our Lord.
R: Hic non dicatur *Flectámus génua,* sed *Orémus.*
 = Here *Flectámus génua* is not said, but *Orémus.*
L: Oratio
 = Prayer
T: ^OMNIPOTENS sempitérne Deus, qui étiam Judáicam perfídiam a tua misericórdia non repéllis : exáudi preces nostras, quas pro illíus pópuli obcæcatióne deférimus; ut ágnita veritátis tuæ luce, quæ Christus est, a suis ténebris eruántur : Per eúmdem Dóminum. {℟.} Amen.
 = Almighty and everlasting God, who do not drive away from Your mercy even the faithlessness of the Jews, hear the prayers we offer for the blindness of that people, that, acknowledging the light of Your truth, which is Christ, they may be delivered from their darkness: through the same Lord. {℟.} Amen.
T: ^OREMUS et pro pagánis, ut Deus omnípotens áuferat iniquitátem a córdibus eórum; ut relíctis idólis suis, convertántur ad Deum vivum et verum, et únicum Fílium ejus Jesum Christum Deum et Dóminum nostrum : Orémus. Flectámus génua. Leváte.
 = Let us pray also for the pagans, that almighty God may take away iniquity from their hearts, that, forsaking their idols, they may be converted to the living and true God, and to His only Son Jesus Christ our God and Lord. Let us pray. Let us kneel. Arise.
L: Oratio
 = Prayer
T: ^OMNIPOTENS sempitérne Deus, qui non mortem peccatórum, sed vitam semper inquíris; súscipe propítius oratiónem nostram : et líbera eos ab idolórum cultúra; et ággrega Ecclésiæ tuæ sanctæ, ad laudem et glóriam nóminis tui : Per Dóminum. {℟.} Amen.
 = Almighty and everlasting God, who seek not the death but always the life of sinners, mercifully receive our prayer, deliver them from the worship of idols, and gather them into Your holy Church, to the praise and glory of Your name: through our Lord. {℟.} Amen.

INC: Quad6f_c
